Why the fuck are you here?

251
00:15:42,196 --> 00:15:43,359
There's been a complaint
about your music.

252
00:15:43,660 --> 00:15:45,320
It's shit.

253
00:15:45,324 --> 00:15:46,408
Come on. We gotta go.

254
00:15:47,493 --> 00:15:48,702
Come on!

255
00:15:58,587 --> 00:15:59,713
Are you in charge?

256
00:15:59,797 --> 00:16:02,049
Show us your CCTV footage
from 20 minutes ago.

257
00:16:08,055 --> 00:16:09,431
Um, so.

258
00:16:09,515 --> 00:16:11,767
Do you w-want to talk
about what just happened?

259
00:16:11,767 --> 00:16:14,144
Well, we were too late is what happened.

260
00:16:14,228 --> 00:16:15,729
No. I... I... I meant us.

261
00:16:16,772 --> 00:16:20,192
I think we should talk about
how we evade MI5 security, Min.

262
00:16:21,110 --> 00:16:23,070
Well, it turns out we
evade them by kissing.

263
00:16:23,070 --> 00:16:25,656
There's not gonna be any "us" if
we don't stay ahead of the Dogs

264
00:16:25,656 --> 00:16:27,699
and work out what the
fuck Black was up to.

265
00:16:27,783 --> 00:16:30,994
Yes, of course. But once,
um... once that's sorted...

266
00:16:32,037 --> 00:16:33,789
"us" could still be a thing?

267
00:16:33,789 --> 00:16:35,958
Less likely every time you bring it up.

268
00:16:42,339 --> 00:16:43,382
Hey, come on.

269
00:16:45,717 --> 00:16:47,302
They might let us share a cell.

270
00:16:52,015 --> 00:16:55,060
God. We really, really are fucked.

271
00:16:55,978 --> 00:16:57,146
There.

272
00:16:58,522 --> 00:16:59,690
Yeah, that's him.

273
00:17:03,485 --> 00:17:04,695
Out.

274
00:17:05,362 --> 00:17:07,781
Now. Three. Two.

275
00:17:14,287 --> 00:17:15,538
Yeah, here we go.

276
00:17:21,836 --> 00:17:23,922
- Duffy.
- He's using that ID you gave me.

277
00:17:24,006 --> 00:17:25,798
Booked a 06:00 a.m. flight to Istanbul.

278
00:17:26,383 --> 00:17:28,677
- Are you sure?
- I'm looking at the CCTV right now.

279
00:17:28,761 --> 00:17:31,013
His face is obscured, but it's Lamb.

280
00:17:32,389 --> 00:17:34,308
- We're off to Gatwick.
- Duffy!

281
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,101
Hold on.

282
00:17:38,103 --> 00:17:40,230
Look at this.

283
00:17:41,899 --> 00:17:44,067
Oh, you dirty bastard.

284
00:17:44,151 --> 00:17:45,152
What?

285
00:17:45,152 --> 00:17:46,925
He's also booked flights from Heathrow,

286
00:17:46,926 --> 00:17:48,989
Stansted, London City, Birmingham,

287
00:17:49,615 --> 00:17:51,909
and Manchester. He knows
we'll have to cover 'em all.

288
00:17:51,909 --> 00:17:54,703
- He's drawing us off.
- Yeah, while he runs for a ferry.

289
00:17:54,787 --> 00:17:56,955
No. I know where he's going.

290
00:18:00,584 --> 00:18:01,710
Oh, God.

291
00:18:23,565 --> 00:18:26,360
Whoever you are, back off. I'm armed.

292
00:18:27,361 --> 00:18:29,446
- No, you're not.
- Lamb?

293
00:18:30,239 --> 00:18:32,157
Come on. Open up.

294
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:38,413
Now.

295
00:18:41,375 --> 00:18:43,710
It... It's the middle of the night.

296
00:18:43,794 --> 00:18:45,879
You can't just show up unannounced.

297
00:18:45,963 --> 00:18:47,756
No. Leave the light off.

298
00:18:50,175 --> 00:18:51,385
What do you want?

299
00:18:52,344 --> 00:18:53,804
Fallen off the wagon, have we?

300
00:18:53,804 --> 00:18:55,973
Oh, it's actually a water bottle.

301
00:18:56,473 --> 00:18:58,058
You've probably never seen one.

302
00:18:59,017 --> 00:19:00,018
Get dressed.

303
00:19:00,978 --> 00:19:03,605
- I live here. You can't tell me...
- Just get dressed!

304
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:13,198
Where are we going?

305
00:19:15,993 --> 00:19:16,994
Where are we going?

306
00:19:16,994 --> 00:19:19,121
- What are you doing?
- I'll tell you on the way.

307
00:19:19,121 --> 00:19:20,956
We just gotta move
fast. The Dogs are on us.

308
00:19:21,582 --> 00:19:24,418
Why are they after me?
I've not done anything.

309
00:19:25,335 --> 00:19:27,546
Well, nothing they'd be able to trace.

310
00:19:29,298 --> 00:19:30,924
We gotta keep switching vehicles.

311
00:19:36,638 --> 00:19:40,476
You can't hot-wire any of these.
You need to hack the alarm system.

312
00:19:41,602 --> 00:19:43,228
I can help with that
for the right price.

313
00:19:44,646 --> 00:19:45,981
Oh, come on.

314
00:19:45,981 --> 00:19:47,065
I'll go analog.

315
00:19:52,654 --> 00:19:55,657
I'll have a bacon double cheeseburger...

316
00:19:55,741 --> 00:19:58,994
- Yeah?
- ... chips, a can of Fanta

317
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:01,455
and...

318
00:20:02,664 --> 00:20:04,958
- You just got Kit Kats and TWIX, yeah?
- Just that, thanks.

319
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:09,421
Listen.

320
00:20:11,465 --> 00:20:13,092
If you're in any kind
of personal trouble,

321
00:20:14,051 --> 00:20:17,012
I just want you to know
I couldn't give a fuck.

322
00:20:17,096 --> 00:20:18,889
And I don't want to be dragged into it.

323
00:20:18,889 --> 00:20:20,182
Yeah, you're already in it.

324
00:20:20,182 --> 00:20:21,475
Wha...

325
00:20:26,105 --> 00:20:28,023
Fuck! Whoa!

326
00:20:31,276 --> 00:20:32,277
Fuck!

327
00:20:34,947 --> 00:20:36,073
Yeah?

328
00:20:36,073 --> 00:20:38,158
We have Loy downstairs for you, ma'am.

329
00:20:38,742 --> 00:20:39,993
Oh, I'll be right down.

330
00:21:05,310 --> 00:21:06,562
Ma'am.

331
00:21:24,079 --> 00:21:25,122
Hello.

332
00:21:27,291 --> 00:21:29,793
Would you excuse me a minute? I just...

333
00:21:29,877 --> 00:21:33,839
It is relentless up there.

334
00:21:33,839 --> 00:21:36,550
- I can imagine.
- Oh, no, you can't.

335
00:21:37,176 --> 00:21:38,469
None of you can.

336
00:21:41,138 --> 00:21:43,474
How does it feel to be
back here at the Park?

337
00:21:44,433 --> 00:21:47,186
Well, this isn't really the Park I knew.

338
00:21:47,186 --> 00:21:48,631
I mean, I've never been down here.

339
00:21:48,632 --> 00:21:51,064
I didn't know we had rooms like this.

340
00:21:51,148 --> 00:21:52,524
Not many people do.

341
00:21:53,025 --> 00:21:54,818
That's why I chose it for you.

342
00:21:56,153 --> 00:21:57,863
I don't want anyone to know you're here.

343
00:22:01,658 --> 00:22:03,030
Um, m... my wife knows I'm here...

344
00:22:03,031 --> 00:22:05,162
at the Park...

345
00:22:05,662 --> 00:22:07,956
She still thinks you
work here, doesn't she?

346
00:22:09,625 --> 00:22:11,251
I've been trying to
find the right moment.

347
00:22:11,335 --> 00:22:13,462
It's been a year.

348
00:22:14,254 --> 00:22:16,215
Your little boy must be, what, six?

349
00:22:16,715 --> 00:22:19,093
And Evie, seven?

350
00:22:19,093 --> 00:22:20,594
No, eight.

351
00:22:21,470 --> 00:22:24,264
They must love the idea
their daddy's James Bond.

352
00:22:24,890 --> 00:22:27,684
I understand why you don't
want anyone to know the truth.

353
00:22:27,768 --> 00:22:29,895
Is that what this is about?
Me lying to my family?

354
00:22:29,895 --> 00:22:32,231
You lied to the investigators
first, didn't you?

355
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:34,942
I panicked.

356
00:22:34,942 --> 00:22:38,987
Said you didn't send the email,
even though it came under your login.

357
00:22:40,989 --> 00:22:41,990
Do you want to read it?

358
00:22:43,242 --> 00:22:45,327
- Uh, not really.
- I think you should.

359
00:22:51,375 --> 00:22:54,044
"Anyone else surprised
by Tearney's outfit?

360
00:22:54,795 --> 00:22:56,630
ISIS chic."

361
00:22:56,630 --> 00:22:58,132
"Maybe she's undercover?"

362
00:22:58,674 --> 00:23:01,927
Uh, she wore a shawl
at a press conference.

363
00:23:01,927 --> 00:23:04,430
It... It... It looked
a bit like... like...

364
00:23:05,889 --> 00:23:06,890
Mmm.

365
00:23:07,599 --> 00:23:09,518
You used a service email chain

366
00:23:09,518 --> 00:23:11,925
to imply that the
head of MI5 was working

367
00:23:11,925 --> 00:23:14,273
undercover for a terrorist organization.

368
00:23:14,273 --> 00:23:15,899
But it was meant as a joke.

369
00:23:17,192 --> 00:23:20,195
But it's a pattern of behavior, Struan.

370
00:23:20,279 --> 00:23:21,947
Joking around.

371
00:23:22,865 --> 00:23:25,451
Undermining your superiors.

372
00:23:25,451 --> 00:23:28,787
Questioning the line of command.
Not taking your job seriously.

373
00:23:28,871 --> 00:23:31,748
And what we do here is very serious.

374
00:23:34,168 --> 00:23:36,086
So if you were to come back
here to work at the Park,

375
00:23:36,170 --> 00:23:38,505
I need to know that you
have learnt your lesson.

376
00:23:39,047 --> 00:23:40,048
Absolutely!

377
00:23:40,716 --> 00:23:41,967
I can't promise anything.

378
00:23:44,636 --> 00:23:46,847
You probably know how many
people have made it back

379
00:23:46,847 --> 00:23:50,184
from Slough House to upstairs
here at Regent's Park. Hmm?

380
00:23:50,809 --> 00:23:52,019
None.

381
00:23:53,312 --> 00:23:54,646
It's not impossible.

382
00:23:59,067 --> 00:24:01,361
Have you seen anything
unusual at Slough House,

383
00:24:01,445 --> 00:24:02,988
any activity?

384
00:24:09,411 --> 00:24:10,412
No.

385
00:24:13,290 --> 00:24:14,625
Uh...

386
00:24:17,628 --> 00:24:18,837
I don't think so.

387
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:25,177
What sort of unusual activity?

388
00:24:27,387 --> 00:24:29,264
It's a shame you
haven't noticed anything.

389
00:24:29,348 --> 00:24:30,808
I was relying on you.

390
00:24:32,893 --> 00:24:34,394
You see, I have a problem.

391
00:24:35,354 --> 00:24:36,814
Quite a big problem.

392
00:24:37,606 --> 00:24:40,109
How would you like to
be part of the solution?

393
00:24:43,946 --> 00:24:46,198
Slow down! This isn't Mario Kart!

394
00:24:46,198 --> 00:24:48,242
Can you get Alan Black's
service record up on that?

395
00:24:48,242 --> 00:24:50,702
Can you stop wasting my time
with rhetorical questions?

396
00:24:52,788 --> 00:24:55,082
Can you just do it please?
Or whatever the magic word is.

397
00:24:55,082 --> 00:24:57,501
How did you find me?
Those are the magic words.

398
00:24:57,501 --> 00:24:59,378
Stop dicking around, Roddy. Just do it.

399
00:25:00,587 --> 00:25:02,506
No, but this is a major security breach.

400
00:25:02,506 --> 00:25:04,716
I need to review protocols
so it doesn't happen again.

401
00:25:04,800 --> 00:25:07,553
You overlooked a massive
weak spot in your defenses.

402
00:25:07,553 --> 00:25:08,887
Impossible.

403
00:25:08,971 --> 00:25:11,056
I hacked the personnel
database at the Park.

404
00:25:11,140 --> 00:25:12,850
I-I changed my address.

405
00:25:12,850 --> 00:25:15,936
My phone, my Internet, my
bills, even my bank account

406
00:25:15,936 --> 00:25:18,939
are all linked to false IDs
that rotate every 24 hours.

407
00:25:18,939 --> 00:25:21,358
I'm so far off the grid, I don't
even know where the grid is.

408
00:25:21,442 --> 00:25:22,443
Lamb followed you home.

409
00:25:24,445 --> 00:25:25,529
When the fuck?

410
00:25:25,529 --> 00:25:27,322
I don't know, but he told everyone.

411
00:25:29,533 --> 00:25:30,533
Black! Come on.

412
00:25:32,953 --> 00:25:34,663
You worked with Black, didn't you?

413
00:25:35,706 --> 00:25:37,207
- Roddy!
- Yeah!

414
00:25:37,291 --> 00:25:39,835
What was Black doing in
that house with Hassan Ahmed?

415
00:25:39,835 --> 00:25:42,171
Any clues in anything he said or did?

416
00:25:42,171 --> 00:25:43,922
Yeah, on the last day
he said, "Fuck you.

417
00:25:44,006 --> 00:25:46,508
I'm off to kidnap an Asian kid
and behead him for the Union Jack."

418
00:25:46,592 --> 00:25:48,677
Fuck's sake, Roddy. Right, fine. Okay?

419
00:25:49,595 --> 00:25:51,305
You drive like a maniac, you know.

420
00:25:55,517 --> 00:25:57,686
- That's him.
- Eyes on the road!

421
00:25:57,770 --> 00:25:58,771
Look ahead!

422
00:25:58,771 --> 00:26:01,064
I've definitely seen
him somewhere. Come on.

423
00:26:02,024 --> 00:26:03,549
We never crossed paths at Slough House.

424
00:26:03,549 --> 00:26:05,152
I think he left before
I joined the Park.

425
00:26:05,152 --> 00:26:07,112
This has literally
nothing to do with me.

426
00:26:07,988 --> 00:26:09,448
Do you recognize him?

427
00:26:10,324 --> 00:26:14,369
Alan Black. Left Slough
House soon after I arrived.

428
00:26:14,995 --> 00:26:16,205
Seen him since?

429
00:26:22,002 --> 00:26:23,003
You sure?

430
00:26:24,296 --> 00:26:27,341
You haven't seen him recently
in the company of Jackson Lamb?

431
00:26:30,344 --> 00:26:32,471
Uh, well, not since he left.

432
00:26:40,854 --> 00:26:43,107
Then you're not part of
the solution then, are you?

433
00:26:43,107 --> 00:26:44,900
You're just another problem.

434
00:26:59,540 --> 00:27:02,084
What are you doing?
This isn't Blake's grave.

435
00:27:02,084 --> 00:27:03,585
I just need to know that she's okay.

436
00:27:03,669 --> 00:27:04,878
- All right?
- Why?

437
00:27:05,796 --> 00:27:07,256
She can't help you now!

438
00:27:07,965 --> 00:27:10,467
You'll be lucky if you get ten
minutes before the Park get here!

439
00:27:10,551 --> 00:27:12,886
I'll be out in five. Just
leave the engine running!

440
00:27:12,970 --> 00:27:13,971
Fuck.

441
00:27:31,405 --> 00:27:33,699
You have two new messages.

442
00:27:33,699 --> 00:27:35,492
Message one.

443
00:27:35,576 --> 00:27:38,996
This is Diana Taverner. You need
to come to the Park straightaway.

444
00:27:38,996 --> 00:27:40,914
Jackson Lamb's gone rogue.

445
00:27:41,665 --> 00:27:43,625
Message two.

446
00:27:43,709 --> 00:27:47,379
Catherine, Diana Taverner again. I
really need you to come to the Park.

447
00:27:47,463 --> 00:27:49,214
There are things about
Charles Partner's death

448
00:27:49,298 --> 00:27:50,799
that Lamb hasn't told you.

449
00:27:50,883 --> 00:27:52,092
Call me.

450
00:28:00,934 --> 00:28:01,934
Morning.

451
00:28:05,689 --> 00:28:08,317
I picked up your blue suit.

452
00:28:10,819 --> 00:28:12,821
You could wear that today if you fancy.

453
00:28:15,616 --> 00:28:17,534
- Charles?
- What's taking so long?

454
00:28:18,744 --> 00:28:19,870
Get out of my bedroom.

455
00:28:19,870 --> 00:28:22,790
What, you think I want to
catch you in your underwear?

456
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:25,083
I imagine you'd like that.

457
00:28:25,167 --> 00:28:28,962
Almost as much as I'd like to
see you in your nylon Y-fronts.

458
00:28:29,546 --> 00:28:30,839
Come on.

459
00:28:30,923 --> 00:28:31,965
Now!

460
00:28:41,475 --> 00:28:43,519
What was Taverner talking about?

461
00:28:43,519 --> 00:28:45,395
What don't I know about Charles's death?

462
00:28:45,479 --> 00:28:47,898
She's... ... screwing with your head.

463
00:28:47,898 --> 00:28:51,235
Look, you could leave with me now
or with less friendly people later.

464
00:28:51,235 --> 00:28:52,319
It's up to you.

465
00:28:59,952 --> 00:29:01,829
No, leave... leave the phone.

466
00:29:14,925 --> 00:29:16,130
Hi. Sorry, can you, uh...

467
00:29:16,131 --> 00:29:18,178
Can you tell me which
room Sidonie Baker's in?

468
00:29:18,804 --> 00:29:20,222
It's immediate family only.

469
00:29:20,222 --> 00:29:21,765
Yeah, I'm her stepbrother.

470
00:29:21,849 --> 00:29:23,517
Can you sign in on the screen?

471
00:29:24,893 --> 00:29:25,894
Yeah, yeah.

472
00:29:36,780 --> 00:29:39,741
- Great. Which room?
- ICU room 4.

473
00:29:39,825 --> 00:29:41,869
- End of the corridor on the right.
- Great, thank you.

474
00:29:52,129 --> 00:29:53,255
Pierce?

475
00:29:56,592 --> 00:29:57,843
Baker has a visitor.

476
00:30:00,262 --> 00:30:02,139
What the fuck is he doing there?

477
00:30:02,639 --> 00:30:03,974
Who can get there fastest?

478
00:30:05,517 --> 00:30:08,228
Cartwright's back at
the hospital. Get him.

479
00:30:08,312 --> 00:30:09,354
With pleasure.

480
00:30:13,734 --> 00:30:15,027
Oh, do fuck off.

481
00:30:16,779 --> 00:30:18,530
It's River, isn't it?

482
00:30:18,614 --> 00:30:21,408
Has he gone off the rails,
and now we're paying the price?

483
00:30:21,492 --> 00:30:23,118
Well, not a million miles off.

484
00:30:23,869 --> 00:30:26,288
Baker's been hurt. Moody's dead.

485
00:30:27,122 --> 00:30:29,458
There's probably a C
& C out on all of us.

486
00:30:29,458 --> 00:30:30,709
Fuckers.

487
00:30:30,793 --> 00:30:32,544
How badly hurt is Sid?

488
00:30:32,628 --> 00:30:36,465
Uh, not as badly hurt as Moody's
dead. Did you catch that bit?

489
00:30:36,465 --> 00:30:40,677
Jed Moody was always going
to end badly, but I like Sid.

490
00:31:08,288 --> 00:31:09,289
Busy night?

491
00:31:09,373 --> 00:31:11,583
You angling for overtime, Nick?

492
00:31:11,667 --> 00:31:13,035
You're talking to the wrong bloke.

493
00:31:13,035 --> 00:31:14,670
Need to know if you're
carrying a weapon.

494
00:31:14,670 --> 00:31:15,754
Nope.

495
00:31:15,838 --> 00:31:18,595
- I'll have to check that. Spread 'em, please.
- Please, Nick, shut the kid up.

496
00:31:18,596 --> 00:31:21,427
Come on, it's embarrassing.
You're a pro.

497
00:31:21,427 --> 00:31:24,012
You can tell from the fold of
my clothes I'm not carrying.

498
00:31:24,096 --> 00:31:27,182
- I'm afraid you don't get a choice...
- If he takes another step towards me,

499
00:31:27,266 --> 00:31:29,768
he'll be frisking me with broken wrists.

500
00:31:37,568 --> 00:31:38,569
Come on.

501
00:31:49,538 --> 00:31:51,707
Webb, you can drive.

502
00:31:52,291 --> 00:31:54,001
Ms. Standish, you're up front.

503
00:31:54,710 --> 00:31:56,920
Lamb, you're in the back with me.

504
00:32:08,140 --> 00:32:09,141
Come on.

505
00:32:09,767 --> 00:32:11,602
Are you serious?

506
00:32:22,112 --> 00:32:25,574
Time's up, Cartwright. Screw all this.

507
00:33:07,407 --> 00:33:08,450
Come on.

